        "readability": 6.5,
        "reasons": {
          "overall_mobile": "Two complete assisted runs provided a coherent recovery/combat/upload loop with clear progression and polished atmosphere. Missed acquisition, scene occlusion and turning correction create noticeable friction; continuous mobile feel remains unassessed.",
          "controls": "Large labeled controls and native two-contact MOVE/FIRE worked in sampled engagements. FIRE drag and scene turning responded; DASH visibly activated. Acquisition after displacement and right-edge overlay required correction. Both terminal evade counts zero. Cannot grade continuous holds or physical thumb ergonomics.",
          "gameplay": "Recovery, numbered-coil combat and deck upload gave distinct visible goals and concrete feedback. Assisted travel made progress approachable; manual guards and damage provided combat coverage. Route success alone says little about free navigation, sustained challenge or enjoyment.",
          "presentation": "Strong teal/amber visual identity, rain, wet surfaces, architecture and clean title/result screens. Software rendering limits performance and fidelity conclusions.",
          "usability": "Context-sensitive ROUTE/APPROACH text, path arrows, mission checks, percentages and explicit assist stats helped. Dense right-side overlays sometimes compete with scene targeting.",
          "readability": "Health, ammo, large control labels and objective names readable at 844x390. Small environmental text, dark distant guards and threat overlay occlusion were weaker."
        }
