        "reasons": {
          "overallMobile": "Coherent and accessible complete mission in portrait, strong feedback and assistance, with narrow-view threat tracking and crowded control/scene space. Two assisted wins alone do not determine the grade.",
          "controls": "Labeled MOVE/FIRE drag, scene swipe and DASH registered. Tap aim helped visible patrol engagement. Edge targets and projection changes require care; continuous hold comfort and physical ergonomics unassessed.",
          "gameplay": "Recovery-to-Custodian-to-upload sequence provides clear progression; OPEN/ARMOR and damage make timing and threats visible. Much travel was assisted, and repeated route holds felt procedurally simple in this sampled mode; unaided depth and sustained enjoyment unassessed.",
          "presentation": "Rain, teal/gold lighting, industrial silhouettes, weapon and polished title/result panels form a consistent atmosphere. Software-WebGL cannot establish phone visual performance.",
          "usability": "Clear objective checkmarks, contextual HOLD APPROACH/FACE COILS, extraction map and progress bar explain next actions; multiple simultaneous warnings and controls still demand attention.",
          "readability": "High contrast HUD and large control labels worked at 390x844. Distant sentinels, small Roman coil labels, tiny map legend and text over dark moving scenery were harder; portrait limits lateral awareness."
        }
